{
  "message": "Thank you, John. To help improve your mobile data speed, I’ll guide you through a few simple steps. Let’s start by making sure your phone is set to use the fastest available network (4G/5G).

Please follow this step:

1. On your phone, set your network mode preference to '4G/5G preferred'.

Let me know once you’ve done this, or if you need instructions on how to do it."
}

{
  "message": "Great job! Next, let's make sure your mobile data is turned ON. Please check your phone's settings and ensure that mobile data is enabled. If you're not sure how to do this, let me know and I can guide you through the steps. Once you've confirmed that mobile data is ON, please let me know."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, that's correct! When Airplane Mode is ON, it turns off all wireless connections, including mobile data. Please turn Airplane Mode OFF first. Once you've done that, check if your mobile data is working better. Let me know when Airplane Mode is off, and if you still have any issues, we'll continue troubleshooting together."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the update! Now that Airplane Mode is off and you see 5G, let's make sure your mobile data is enabled. Please turn ON your mobile data in your phone's settings. Once you've done that, let me know if your internet is working or if you still notice any issues."
}

{
  "message": "Great! Now, please try using the internet on your phone—open a website or an app that needs internet and see if it loads quickly. If it works well, your issue may be resolved. If it’s still slow or not working, let me know, and I’ll guide you through the next steps to further improve your connection."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for letting me know. Since your mobile data is on and you see 5G, but the internet still isn’t working, let’s check if your phone’s data roaming is enabled. Sometimes, if you’re outside your usual coverage area, data roaming needs to be on for internet access.\n\nPlease check your phone’s settings and make sure data roaming is enabled. If you’re not sure how to do this, let me know and I can guide you. Once you’ve checked or enabled data roaming, let me know if the internet starts working."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking. I found that your line did not have roaming enabled on our end, even though it was enabled on your phone. I have now enabled roaming for your line. Please try using your mobile data again. If it still doesn't work, try restarting your phone. Let me know if your internet is working now or if you need further assistance."
}

{
  "message": "You're very welcome, John! I'm glad to hear your internet speed is excellent and everything is working perfectly now. If you ever need help again, feel free to reach out. Have a great day and enjoy your fast connection!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your service issue. To get started, I need to verify your account. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Your line ending in 2002 is currently suspended, which is why you are seeing 'No Service.' The suspension is due to an overdue bill of $65. I have just sent you a payment request for this overdue bill. Please check your payment requests and let me know once you have accepted it, so I can help you complete the payment and restore your service."
}

{
  "message": "Your payment has been received and your overdue bill is now marked as paid. I have resumed your service for the line ending in 2002. Please reboot your phone to restore your cellular service. If you still experience issues after rebooting, let me know and I can assist you further."
}

{
  "message": "Since your status bar is showing Airplane Mode, your phone will not be able to connect to the cellular network. Please turn off Airplane Mode on your device. Once Airplane Mode is off, check if you have signal. Let me know if you still have issues after doing this."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for turning off Airplane Mode. Since you still see 'No Signal' and data is disabled, the next step is to check your SIM card status. Please check your SIM card status on your device and let me know if it shows as active, missing, or locked."
}

{
  "message": "Since your phone is not detecting the SIM card, please try removing the SIM card from your phone and then reinserting it. After reseating the SIM card, check if your phone recognizes it and if you regain service. Let me know the result."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for trying to reseat the SIM card. Since your phone still does not detect the SIM and you continue to have no service, this may indicate a hardware or SIM card issue that I am unable to resolve remotely. I will transfer you to a human agent who can assist you further with this problem."
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON."
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS issue. First, I need to verify your account for security purposes. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for verifying your information, John. To help resolve your MMS issue, I’ll need you to perform a few quick checks and actions on your phone. First, please check if Airplane Mode is currently enabled on your device. If it is, please turn it off. You can do this by toggling Airplane Mode off in your phone’s settings or control panel. Let me know once you’ve done this, or if Airplane Mode was already off."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please go ahead and turn Airplane Mode off now. This will re-enable your phone's wireless connections, which are necessary for sending MMS messages. Let me know once you have turned it off."
}

{
  "message": "Great! Next, let's make sure your phone is set to use the best available network for MMS. Please set your network mode preference to '4G/5G preferred' in your phone's settings. This will help ensure your device is using a network that supports MMS. Let me know once you've done this, or if you need instructions on how to change this setting."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for updating your network mode. Now, please try sending an MMS message to see if the issue is resolved. If you are still unable to send MMS, let me know and we can continue troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for letting me know. The next step is to check your phone's APN settings, as incorrect settings can prevent MMS from working. Please check your APN settings and let me know if the MMSC URL is set. If you need instructions on how to check this, let me know your phone's make and model."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking your APN settings. Next, let's check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled on your device, as it can sometimes interfere with MMS. Please check your phone's Wi-Fi Calling status and let me know if it is currently ON. If it is, please turn it OFF and then try sending an MMS again."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming that Wi-Fi Calling is off. Next, let's check if your messaging app has the necessary permissions to send MMS. Please check the app permissions for your messaging app and make sure it has both 'storage' and 'SMS' permissions enabled. Let me know if either of these permissions is missing, or if both are already enabled."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming the app permissions. Since the basic settings and permissions are correct, let's try restarting your device. Please reboot your phone now, as this can often resolve temporary issues with messaging services. After your phone restarts, try sending an MMS again and let me know if it works."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. I see that your data usage for this billing cycle has exceeded your plan's data limit, which can prevent MMS from working since MMS requires mobile data. You have used 15.1GB out of your 15GB limit. Would you like to add more data (up to 2GB) to your line for $2.00 per GB so you can resume sending MMS messages? If so, please let me know how much data you would like to add."
}

{
  "message": "2.0 GB of data has been successfully added to your line for $4.00. Please try sending an MMS message again now. If you still experience issues, let me know and we can continue troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear that your MMS messages are working again! If you have any other questions or need further assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you troubleshoot your MMS issue. First, I’ll need to verify your account for technical support. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for providing your information, John. To help resolve your MMS issue, I’ll need you to perform a few quick checks and actions on your phone. Let’s start by making sure Airplane Mode is turned off, as this can block all messaging services. Please use the toggle_airplane_mode() action on your device now. Let me know once you’ve done this, and we’ll continue with the next steps."
}

{
  "message": "Great, thank you! Next, let's make sure your phone is set to use the best available network for MMS. Please set your network mode preference to '4G/5G Preferred' by using the set_network_mode_preference(mode=4g_5g_preferred) action on your device. Let me know once this is done so we can proceed."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you! Now, let's ensure your messaging app has the necessary permissions to send and receive MMS. Please grant the 'storage' permission to your messaging app by using the grant_app_permission(app_name=messaging, permission=storage) action. Let me know once you've completed this step."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you! Next, let's make sure your mobile data is turned on, as MMS requires an active data connection. Please use the toggle_data() action to enable mobile data on your device. Let me know once this is done so we can continue troubleshooting if needed."
}

{
  "message": "Thanks for turning on mobile data. If you are currently traveling outside your home network or in a different country, MMS may require data roaming to be enabled. If this applies to you, please use the toggle_roaming() action to turn on data roaming. Let me know once this is done, or if you are not traveling, let me know so we can proceed with other troubleshooting steps."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for enabling data roaming. Please try sending an MMS message now to see if the issue is resolved. If you are still unable to send MMS, let me know and we can continue with further troubleshooting steps."
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear that your MMS messaging is working again! If you have any other questions or need further assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS (picture message) issue. First, I need to identify your account to provide the best support. Could you please provide your phone number, customer ID, or your full name and date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. I have identified your account. To help fix your MMS (picture message) issue, I’ll need to guide you through a few quick checks and steps on your phone. First, can you confirm if you are able to make regular calls and use mobile data (for example, browsing the web) on your phone right now?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the details. Since your phone is currently connected to a 2G network, this can prevent MMS (picture messages) from working properly. Let's try switching your phone to prefer 4G or 5G networks, which are required for MMS. Please set your network mode preference to '4G/5G preferred' in your phone's settings. Let me know once you've done this, or if you need instructions on how to do it."
}

{
  "message": "Great! Now that your phone is connected to a 5G network with a better signal, let's make sure your messaging app has the necessary permissions to send MMS. Please grant the 'SMS' permission to your messaging app in your phone's settings. Let me know once you've done this, or if you need help with the steps."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for letting me know. You will not lose your photos by changing these settings or permissions. Let's continue troubleshooting. The next step is to check if your messaging app has the necessary 'storage' permission, which you mentioned is already granted. Now, let's make sure your phone's APN (Access Point Name) settings are correct, as incorrect APN settings can prevent MMS from working. Could you please check your APN settings and let me know if you see an MMSC (Multimedia Messaging Service Center) URL listed? If you're unsure how to check, I can guide you through the steps."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking. Since your APN name and MMSC URL are set, they appear to be correct. Let's try one more thing: sometimes, changes to network or APN settings require a device restart to take effect. Please restart your phone now. After it powers back on, try sending a picture message again. Let me know if it works or if you still have trouble."
}

{
  "message": "I understand this is frustrating, and I assure you that the troubleshooting steps we’re taking will not delete your photos or important data. Let’s try another step: sometimes Wi-Fi Calling can interfere with sending MMS. Could you please check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled on your phone? If it is, please turn it off and then try sending a picture message again. Let me know what you find or if you need help with the steps."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking that. Since Wi-Fi Calling is off and we've already checked your network, permissions, and APN settings, let's try one more thing: sometimes background data restrictions or Data Saver mode can interfere with MMS. Please check if Data Saver mode is enabled on your phone. If it is, please turn it off and try sending a picture message again. Let me know if you need help finding this setting."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. I have just enabled data roaming on your line, which can sometimes help with MMS delivery even if you are not traveling. Please restart your phone one more time, then try sending a picture message again. Let me know if this resolves the issue or if you still need help."
}

{
  "message": "I'm very glad to hear that your picture messages are working now! If you have any other questions or need help in the future, feel free to reach out. Thank you for your patience, and have a great day!"
}
